# A publish target — copy to deploy/web/targets/<name>.env (gitignored) and fill in. No passwords here:
# the SSH/SFTP key is your own, loaded in ssh-agent.
WEB_URL=https://basis.onderling.org
WEB_HOST=ssh.example.org
WEB_USER=onderling
WEB_PORT=22
WEB_PATH=/www/basis.onderling.org
# rsync needs a shell on the host (most VPS/SSH hosting); sftp works on any SFTP-only web host
WEB_MODE=sftp
# only when the app lives under a path of the site (basic hosting tiers without subdomains): the Vite base
# WEB_BASE=/basis/
# Any VITE_ key is passed to the build — a DEPLOYMENT's defaults, which the repo deliberately does not hold.
# The relay this hosted build should use out of the box (a member can still change it in the app):
# VITE_CIRCLE_RELAY_URL=wss://relay.example.org
# The contact this build SHIPS WITH — a person in Contacten from the first launch (the alpha's feedback
# path: the maker's own account). Print it on any device of that account with `/share-my-contact` and paste
# the `onderling-contact://…` line here; it is public information (address, key, handle, primary relay).
# Absent ⇒ no seeded contact. Mobile builds: EXPO_PUBLIC_SEEDED_CONTACT_CARD, the same value.
# VITE_SEEDED_CONTACT_CARD=onderling-contact://…
